WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.303
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for knowing the letters, big and small.

2
00:00:04.753 --> 00:00:11.759
The goal is a child who names all 26 letters, big and small, even in a typeface never seen in the book.

3
00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:18.047
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

4
00:00:18.847 --> 00:00:22.113
This plan is for a child who knows only a few letters.

5
00:00:22.563 --> 00:00:24.692
Or mixes up the letters that look alike.

6
00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:27.835
Or knows the big letters, but not the small ones.

7
00:00:28.285 --> 00:00:32.868
Letters are hard to tell apart. Many are the same shape, turned or flipped.

8
00:00:33.318 --> 00:00:40.378
A child who meets all 26 at once never gets the time to tell them apart. So this plan takes five a day.

9
00:00:41.178 --> 00:00:45.561
Days two, three and four bring five letters a day, big and small together.

10
00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:47.823
Day five is a halfway check.

11
00:00:48.273 --> 00:00:55.637
Then the rest of the letters. Letters that look alike are taught on different days, and only put side by side on day eight.

12
00:00:56.087 --> 00:01:00.769
Day nine is the whole alphabet in order, and day ten is the final check.

13
00:01:01.569 --> 00:01:07.898
There is an alphabet chart in the book, with an animal friend for every letter. Put it up where your child can see it.

14
00:01:08.348 --> 00:01:14.459
This plan teaches the names of the letters. The sounds come next, in our plan Eight Sounds That Stay.

15
00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:20.248
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
